---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import car from '../../data/car.json';

const OCTOPUS_REFERRAL = 'https://share.octopus.energy/lush-spark-49';

const { use, annual_gbp: a, cost_per_mile_p: cpm, replaced, fuel_sensitivity: fs } = car;
const gbp = (n: number) => `£${Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-GB')}`;
const [qashqai, c4] = replaced.cars;

const allCosts = fs.rows.flatMap((r: any) => r.cost);
const lo = Math.min(...allCosts);
const hi = Math.max(...allCosts);
const shade = (v: number) => {
  const k = (v - lo) / (hi - lo);
  if (k > 0.72) return '#5b83e6';
  if (k > 0.45) return '#9ab4f2';
  if (k > 0.22) return '#c9d8f8';
  return '#e8eefc';
};
const ink = (v: number) => ((v - lo) / (hi - lo) > 0.72 ? '#fff' : 'inherit');

// pence per mile, scaled against the thirstiest thing we used to drive
const barMax = cpm.petrol_qashqai;
const bars = [
  { label: 'Enyaq · charged overnight at 7.6p', v: cpm.iog_night, tone: 'accent' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · from solar surplus, at the 12p we give up', v: cpm.solar_surplus_opportunity, tone: 'accent' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · on an ordinary flat tariff', v: cpm.standard_flat, tone: 'mid' },
  { label: 'Enyaq · charged at the day rate', v: cpm.day_rate, tone: 'mid' },
  { label: 'Citroen C4 · diesel', v: cpm.diesel_c4, tone: 'dark' },
  { label: 'Nissan Qashqai · petrol', v: cpm.petrol_qashqai, tone: 'dark' },
];
---

<Base
  title="The car"
  description="A Skoda Enyaq replacing a petrol Qashqai and a diesel Citroen C4. What 10,000 miles a year costs on an overnight tariff against petrol at 167p and diesel at 189p, and how much of the saving is really down to the solar."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>The car</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A <strong>Skoda Enyaq</strong> arrived in <strong>July 2026</strong> and is now the only car
      on the drive. It replaced two: a <strong>petrol Nissan Qashqai 1.6</strong> and a
      {' '}<strong>diesel Citroen C4</strong>, which did roughly half the mileage each. It's the
      biggest new electricity load the house has had, and also one of the biggest savings on this
      site. This page treats those as two separate things.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="note warn">
    <p><strong>Modelled, not measured.</strong> The car isn't metered separately from the house, so
    mileage, efficiency and charging losses here are estimates. The fuel figures use the economy
    we actually got from the two cars (not the manufacturer figures) at UK average pump prices in
    September 2026. We'll replace them with real figures after a full year of charging.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tiles" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Driven</p>
      <span class="figure md">{(use.miles_per_year / 1000).toFixed(0)}k<span class="unit">mi/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">at {use.miles_per_kwh} mi/kWh</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Electricity used</p>
      <span class="figure md">{use.kwh_from_meter.toLocaleString('en-GB')}<span class="unit">kWh</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">off the meter, incl. charging losses</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Fuel it replaces</p>
      <span class="figure md">{gbp(a.fuel_baseline)}<span class="unit">/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">two cars, blended {replaced.blended_pence_per_mile}p a mile</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Saving</p>
      <span class="figure md accent">{gbp(a.saving_total)}<span class="unit">/yr</span></span>
      <p class="note-line">{replaced.blended_pence_per_mile}p a mile down to {cpm.iog_night}p</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>What a mile costs</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    The Qashqai's 1.6 petrol managed about {qashqai.mpg_real} mpg in real use, which at
    {' '}{(qashqai.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p a litre is
    {' '}<strong>{qashqai.pence_per_mile}p a mile</strong>. The C4 diesel did much better at
    {' '}{c4.mpg_real} mpg, but diesel is the dearer fuel now at
    {' '}{(c4.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p, so it still cost
    {' '}<strong>{c4.pence_per_mile}p</strong>. The Enyaq, charged overnight, costs
    {' '}<strong>{cpm.iog_night}p</strong>.
  </p>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="mile-bars">
      {bars.map((b) => (
        <div class="mrow">
          <span class="mlabel">{b.label}</span>
          <span class="mtrack">
            <span class={`mfill ${b.tone}`} style={`width:${(b.v / barMax) * 100}%`}></span>
          </span>
          <span class="mval">{b.v.toFixed(2)}p</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="caption">
      Pence per mile. Even charged in the middle of a weekday at the full day rate, the Enyaq is
      cheaper to run than the diesel was, and half the cost of the petrol.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>How much of this is the solar?</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Very little. Most of the saving comes from the car being electric. Anyone with a driveway and a
    cheap overnight tariff would get most of it without any solar panels at all.
  </p>

  <div class="ledger">
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Petrol and diesel, two cars, 50/50</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.fuel_baseline)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Same miles, electric, on an ordinary flat tariff</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.ev_on_standard_flat)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Saved by going electric at all</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_from_going_electric)}</strong></span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k">Same miles, charged in the overnight window</span>
      <span class="v">{gbp(a.ev_on_iog_night)}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Saved again by the tariff</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_from_the_tariff)}</strong></span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="k"><strong>Total against the old fuel bill</strong></span>
      <span class="v"><strong>{gbp(a.saving_total)}</strong></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>We've left this saving out of the solar payback.</strong> The
    {' '}<a href="/stats/">payback tracker</a> compares the panels and battery against what the
    same electricity would have cost without them. Adding {gbp(a.saving_total)} of avoided fuel
    would make the solar look as if it paid back in half the time. That wouldn't be fair, because
    we'd have saved most of it by buying the same car and plugging it in at an ordinary house, so
    the two are counted separately.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>What if fuel prices change?</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Our electricity price is fixed for twelve months, but pump prices aren't. Diesel is already
    about {(c4.price_per_litre * 100).toFixed(0)}p and edging towards £2. The old fuel bill goes up
    with it and the charging bill stays where it is.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>10,000 miles</th>
          {fs.scenarios.map((s: any) => <th>{s.label}</th>)}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {fs.rows.map((r: any) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{r.what.startsWith('Our') ? <strong>{r.what}</strong> : r.what}</td>
            {r.cost.map((v: number) => (
              <td style={`background:${shade(v)}; color:${ink(v)}; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:0.82rem`}>
                {gbp(v)}
              </td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="lede">
    Against {gbp(a.ev_on_iog_night)} of electricity, every cell in that table is a saving of
    between {gbp(fs.rows[1].cost[0] - a.ev_on_iog_night)} and
    {' '}{gbp(fs.rows[0].cost[2] - a.ev_on_iog_night)} a year. The electric car is cheaper at
    today's fuel prices, and the gap only widens if they rise.
  </p>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Why we don't charge it from the solar</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    Until 22 September the car charged from surplus solar on a granny lead. With export unpaid,
    that was the right call: a spare kWh was worth nothing unless we used it, and every unit that
    went into the car instead of the grid saved the full import price.
  </p>

  <div class="note quiet">
    <p><strong>Now that export pays, we do the opposite.</strong> Exported solar earns 12p and the
    overnight rate is 8p, so it's cheaper to export the solar and charge the car overnight, and
    we keep the difference on every kWh the car takes. Not charging the car from your own
    panels feels odd, so we've written it down here before we get into the habit.
    See <a href="/tariff/">the tariff</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head"><h2>Winter will be tighter</h2></div>
  <p class="lede">
    The car adds about {use.kwh_from_meter.toLocaleString('en-GB')} kWh a year to a house that
    generates about 9,900. In summer that makes little difference. From December the
    {' '}<a href="/heat-pump/">heat pump</a> will be using the same six-hour cheap window, so the
    battery, the car and the heating will all be competing for the same hours. That's mainly a
    scheduling problem for Predbat to handle, and we'll publish how it gets on.
  </p>

  <div class="card referral" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
    <p class="kicker">Charging an EV at home?</p>
    <h2 style="margin:0.2rem 0 0"><img src="/octopus-mark.png" alt="" class="octopus-logo-inline" /> Octopus · we both get £50</h2>
    <p>Most of the saving above comes from the overnight rate. The site has no sponsors, and you
    get the same referral payment we do.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn octopus" href={OCTOPUS_REFERRAL} rel="noopener"><img src="/octopus-mark.png" alt="Octopus Energy" class="octopus-mark" /> Claim £50</a>
      <p class="fine mono">share.octopus.energy/lush-spark-49</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .mile-bars { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
    .mrow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 17rem 1fr 3.4rem; align-items: center; gap: 0.8rem; }
    .mlabel { font-size: 0.86rem; }
    .mtrack { background: var(--track); border-radius: 999px; height: 12px; overflow: hidden; }
    .mfill { display: block; height: 100%; border-radius: 999px; min-width: 6px; background: var(--dark); }
    .mfill.accent { background: var(--accent); }
    .mfill.mid { background: #9ab4f2; }
    .mval { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; text-align: right; color: var(--ink-400); }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .mrow { grid-template-columns: 1fr 3.4rem; }
      .mlabel { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin-bottom: -0.3rem; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
